{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794773003,"nonce":"vwlf6+y41vyYLholUZRj4+uzlB0=","message":"Fourth nAIR slice, 77bbe490: method-table calls have call summaries. Facts.methods maps (receiver value type, slot) to the join of what every function the slot may run writes; summarize_with solves it together with the direct calls, so a table call is an edge to each target and the fixed point settles through it. LICM and GVN look it up through the function (clobbers_all and writes_may_alias now take the Function, since the receiver's type is the type of a value). nAIR records the targets for each table call it lowers (Module::table_calls). Checked on real Haxe (virtuals fixture): Loud.note writes only Counter.hits, Quiet.note and Counter.note write nothing, Main.drive's summary is exactly Counter.hits, and in drive's loop the limit load leaves the loop at O2 with the summary and stays without it; the optimized program still computes 10 and 0. A key that misses (a receiver value whose type a pass has changed to a subtype) falls back to 'anything', which is sound. Still a barrier: closure calls, interface-typed receivers. No timing yet. Next candidates: the nair2hl bridge on objects (so the engines run this), then statics and strings, or constructor shape for SROA on the objects now lowered.","files":null}]}